From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:16:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: offer opt-in systemd text priority prefixes

Add -logtextpriority, disabled by default. Prefix every physical text line with its severity, including subsequent multiline lines. Other encoders retain their own severity schema.

36 logging/event cases and feature_logging pass. A real systemd257 stdout journal stream recognizes priority for all 213 actual daemon file lines and three multiline/error controls; messages match after the collector own trailing ASCII whitespace trimming. The test client uses libsystemd, the daemon does not.

(cherry picked from commit a798067dfa64f6bd9ad769b4af5d01d085243fcb)

